{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e","id":1560713,"title":"D&D and VTM? Vampire: The Masquerade - Bound by Blood (5.5e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-18T11:10:59-07:00","id":1560713,"title":"D&D and VTM? Vampire: The Masquerade - Bound by Blood (5.5e)","content":"Apparently, D&amp;D Beyond is releasing a VTM Dark Ages...module? Adventure? with Kindred class to 5.5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Welcome to the World of Darkness with the new Kindred class for 5.5e. A full vampire class powered by Blood Points, Disciplines, and the ever-clawing Beast inside! Included in this release is a heart-pounding Dark Ages adventure. We will be offering a pre-order of <i>Bound By Blood</i> in June, followed by a release in July. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2195-q3-2026-partnered-content-release-schedule?srsltid=AfmBOoomVpucc2XiOy2F8PNiqPkcglXJNUhRFh87h_kk2ZfvEJ8lbvTZ#vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-55e-preorder-june-release-july\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> for those curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27335,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","user":"Technoma","date":".  Link 06-18-2026, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T15:34:49-07:00","id":1560723,"title":"","content":"I wonder how this would work. One base vamp class with clans being subclasses maybe? But how would you even translate Generation and Blood Potency into the dnd ruleset?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T16:17:07-07:00","id":1560728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1560723#post1560723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how this would work. One base vamp class with clans being subclasses maybe? But how would you even translate Generation and Blood Potency into the dnd ruleset?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Potency I could see being replaced with just character levels, but yeah Generation is the big sticking point. MAYBE having lower generations start off at higher BP / levels a la VTM5? Or simplify things by making Generation a mechanic only for NPCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T17:15:48-07:00","id":1560730,"title":"","content":"You could set up Generation as an Origin Feat that gives you some sort of bonus if you take it. Then with Diablere, and the way it lowers your Generation, could be represented by a Feat that you can take as you level up which gives you various bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T17:41:32-07:00","id":1560732,"title":"","content":"This sounds amazing. I really hope it\u2019s as good as I think it will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T17:47:01-07:00","id":1560733,"title":"","content":"Agree with Origin Feat for Generation, although they may also go for Backgrounds. I wouldn't, but who knows? Or Backgrounds could be clans.<br /> <br /> By Kindred being a class, I suspect it will take a fair amount of artistic license, maybe as much as Monte Cook's WoD, rather than being an actual adaptation, but let's see what we get.<br /> <br /> Though I may need some time before I can see the result by myself legally, since I won't pay any subscription to Hasbro under current conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T17:39:55-07:00","id":1560772,"title":"","content":"I do wonder if they will restrict it to humans or allow you to go nuts with races.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T04:52:22-07:00","id":1560778,"title":"","content":"If it's a class, no reason to not go nuts.<br /> <br /> What I think is if it wouldn't go easier importing some 3.5 rules.<br /> <br /> There it would be possible to convert Kindred to a template and keep the rest of the system free for other character aspects.<br /> <br /> Very technically today the best option would be Kindred as a species, and Disciplines as Feats or something rather than making class progression based on the Curse.<br /> <br /> My personal vision of how VtM works is not like that. The Curse takes a lot of character evolution only because &quot;profession&quot; takes too little, it's less that the game doesn't have Fighters and Rogues, and more that the system doesn't support your class.<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D a normal human can become a threat to a Methuselah because they're that good a Fighter. I think kindred should evolve similarly just with options related to the Curse. Not much different from what was done with some species in Ravenloft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T12:55:46-07:00","id":1560822,"title":"","content":"It's refreshing seeing people talk about this seriously rather than posting vomit emojis and complaining that it ruins their narrow vision of &quot;personal horror&quot; or VTM (as I've seen elsewhere recently). I have never particularly liked D&amp;D rules, but I'll play it if friends offer to run it.<br /> <br /> It always seems weird to me that people get so snobby about how VTM should be played. If this brings in more players, then more power to 'em!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T13:22:33-07:00","id":1560824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1560822#post1560822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's refreshing seeing people talk about this seriously rather than posting vomit emojis and complaining that it ruins their narrow vision of &quot;personal horror&quot; or VTM (as I've seen elsewhere recently). I have never particularly liked D&amp;D rules, but I'll play it if friends offer to run it.<br /> <br /> It always seems weird to me that people get so snobby about how VTM should be played. If this brings in more players, then more power to 'em!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fans can get weirdly married to their visions and headcanons. I know from experience. Personally... Do what makes you happy at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T13:44:32-07:00","id":1560826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1560824#post1560824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fans can get weirdly married to their visions and headcanons. I know from experience. Personally... Do what makes you happy at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree. And being a completist (and curious in any case), I'm likely to pick this up anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T16:26:45-07:00","id":1560838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1560822#post1560822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's refreshing seeing people talk about this seriously rather than posting vomit emojis and complaining that it ruins their narrow vision of &quot;personal horror&quot; or VTM (as I've seen elsewhere recently). I have never particularly liked D&amp;D rules, but I'll play it if friends offer to run it.<br /> <br /> It always seems weird to me that people get so snobby about how VTM should be played. If this brings in more players, then more power to 'em!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've long accepted that if I had a dictionary with pics, the word &quot;Snob&quot; would have the original VtM logo.<br /> <br /> What I find doubling amusing is that a lot of the most pedantic don't really like the system, as they're constantly complaining about rules that are working as intended and their wishes are perfectly delivered by another game.<br /> <br /> Sometimes D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> I'm currently training an AI solely for the purpose of adapting WoD to other systems, so I can have a toolbox of what to play according to the chronicle's proposal and/or available players.<br /> <br /> Also thinking about teaching you guys 3D&amp;T here. You have no idea how interesting it is as a system toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T17:06:12-07:00","id":1560842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1560822#post1560822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's refreshing seeing people talk about this seriously rather than posting vomit emojis and complaining that it ruins their narrow vision of &quot;personal horror&quot; or VTM (as I've seen elsewhere recently). I have never particularly liked D&amp;D rules, but I'll play it if friends offer to run it.<br /> <br /> It always seems weird to me that people get so snobby about how VTM should be played. If this brings in more players, then more power to 'em!</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't get either.<br /> Sure I played &quot;serious&quot;, personal horror games but WoD and VTM is so much more than that. I had fun murderhobo Sabbat pack adventures, ending with diablerizing a Methuselah. I got into estate development that turned into a trip to the Underworld to stop a Wraith group from haunting. Some of my favorite stuff is inherently silly and fun, like EWW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T00:29:02-07:00","id":1560849,"title":"","content":"Now thinking about adaptations I could toy with after I see what they do with D&amp;D Current Pseudo-Edition.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 3.5: detailed systems for the effects of powers, detailed combat styles, granular char gen.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 2024: strategic combat, combat balance.<br /> <br /> M&amp;M 2nd Ed: Stupidly granular control, explore character concepts the lore supports, but no other game could handle. Good modeling of how your powers affect the world.<br /> <br /> 3D&amp;T: surprisingly well adapted in a format that is both conducive of newbie play and fast play without losing much nuance.<br /> <br /> L5R 4th ed: closer to WoD with less complexity on powers, but better handling of conflicts, including social and political conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T13:47:50-07:00","id":1560867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1560826#post1560826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I totally agree. And being a completist (and curious in any case), I'm likely to pick this up anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let us know how it turns out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T04:38:03-07:00","id":1561123,"title":"","content":"I also saw it and read about the Clans that would be allowed in there. (Brujah, Gangrel, Nosferatu, Lasombra, Toreador, and Ventrue) Too bad that Malkavian and Tremere didn't make the list. I wonder how Thaumaturgy would be listed under spells and levels. Not to mention inducing a Madness condition on someone would be interesting roleplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T04:58:56-07:00","id":1561124,"title":"","content":"Conceptually the Tremere are easy to adapt, they're just Wizards (despite in-lore nickname) with their own blood as Magic Implement replacing normal components.<br /> <br /> The mechanical differences are more broader distinctions on magic systems than something in the clan, and I don't think a complete overhaul of magic is the goal.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is complicated by them running vampires as a class, so that's that.<br /> <br /> As for Malkavians, while I will miss it a lot, I'm kinda relieved they won't try if they're not sure they can pull it off, and I'm not a fan of Dementation, so depending on how Disciplines get done it'll be just a matter of putting theirs together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T01:37:36-07:00","id":1562290,"title":"","content":"Any news on this project?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T03:06:16-07:00","id":1562293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562290#post1562290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any news on this project?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://marketplace.dndbeyond.com/category/4IQF87I?icid_medium=organic&amp;icid_source=editorial&amp;icid_campaign=2026_3p_&amp;icid_content=article_2216&amp;pid=DB4IQF87I\" target=\"_blank\">Released</a> yesterday, USD 30 on D&amp;D Beyond.<br /> <br /> There's also a <a href=\"https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2216-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-brings-the\" target=\"_blank\">preview</a> to tell what's inside.<br /> <br /> But as expected, clans as subclasses, and they avoided Tremere.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are apparently tied to clan and you need a feat to get Out of Clans.<br /> <br /> For those who just want a summary:<br /> <br /> 1. All main rules are Class traits. They include Blood Points, resisting the Beast, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. Six Clans: Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue.<br /> <br /> 3. Backgrounds and Feats, they included new Origin Feats. Thin Blood is a Feat for other characters rather than a Class.<br /> <br /> 4. Generation as an Epic Boon... Ok?<br /> <br /> 5. New equipment, nothing I found interesting except maybe the potion of Kindred Vitae.<br /> <br /> 6. Closes with an Adventure for Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> While it's probably compatible across the board, this is written under the assumption that you'll use WoD as setting, not a regular D&amp;D world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-29-2026, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T11:46:58-07:00","id":1562313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562293#post1562293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://marketplace.dndbeyond.com/category/4IQF87I?icid_medium=organic&amp;icid_source=editorial&amp;icid_campaign=2026_3p_&amp;icid_content=article_2216&amp;pid=DB4IQF87I\" target=\"_blank\">Released</a> yesterday, USD 30 on D&amp;D Beyond.<br /> <br /> There's also a <a href=\"https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2216-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-brings-the\" target=\"_blank\">preview</a> to tell what's inside.<br /> <br /> But as expected, clans as subclasses, and they avoided Tremere.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are apparently tied to clan and you need a feat to get Out of Clans.<br /> <br /> For those who just want a summary:<br /> <br /> 1. All main rules are Class traits. They include Blood Points, resisting the Beast, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. Six Clans: Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue.<br /> <br /> 3. Backgrounds and Feats, they included new Origin Feats. Thin Blood is a Feat for other characters rather than a Class.<br /> <br /> 4. Generation as an Epic Boon... Ok?<br /> <br /> 5. New equipment, nothing I found interesting except maybe the potion of Kindred Vitae.<br /> <br /> 6. Closes with an Adventure for Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> While it's probably compatible across the board, this is written under the assumption that you'll use WoD as setting, not a regular D&amp;D world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generation as an epic boon? I've no idea what that means. That's a part of dnd5e I'm not familiar with so could you explain that one? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Disappointed, but not surprised, about the lack of caitiff. They're my go to option in VtM and V5 didn't treat them nicely from what I saw. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T11:53:17-07:00","id":1562314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562313#post1562313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generation as an epic boon? I've no idea what that means. That's a part of dnd5e I'm not familiar with so could you explain that one? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Disappointed, but not surprised, about the lack of caitiff. They're my go to option in VtM and V5 didn't treat them nicely from what I saw. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Progression in 5e only goes up to level 20. Epic Boons are un-leveled benefits applied to level 20 characters that give them some form of progression beyond level 20. Given how powerful a lot of WoD characters are in comparison to D&amp;D characters, it's pretty much necessary to chisel out any details on any given monster character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T12:02:19-07:00","id":1562316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562314#post1562314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Progression in 5e only goes up to level 20. Epic Boons are un-leveled benefits applied to level 20 characters that give them some form of progression beyond level 20. Given how powerful a lot of WoD characters are in comparison to D&amp;D characters, it's pretty much necessary to chisel out any details on any given monster character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Though not sure a lot of WoD characters can compare to the insane stunts of dnd high level mages. They're a special batch of complete nutty stunt. Granted I have a friend who's good at that so maybe my view is skewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T12:21:38-07:00","id":1562317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562316#post1562316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Though not sure a lot of WoD characters can compare to the insane stunts of dnd high level mages. They're a special batch of complete nutty stunt. Granted I have a friend who's good at that so maybe my view is skewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was an extreme exaggeration, especially because they model completely different kinds of stories. D&amp;D is for a game where a group of mortals can feasibly grow enough in skill alone to challenge a Methuselah in their Haven and win.<br /> <br /> Problem is: class level in D&amp;D is about experience. You're not turned or born as a 10th level character. Sometimes, in some editions, you can have Hit Dice that give you more power to represent your innate abilities, but those are not Class Levels.<br /> <br /> An Epic Boon is something you develop late in your career as you continue to amass power and experience. So...<br /> <br /> You can't be Embraced into an Epic Boon, and<br /> You can't Diablerize your way to an Epic Boon.<br /> <br /> Without serious revision in the basic rules, and this doesn't seem to be the goal, this means a newly Embraced Fledgling is 13\u00ba Generation, will remain 13\u00ba Generation until the 20th level, then lower Generation by taking Epic Boons.<br /> <br /> Unless the class has some very specialized way of handling Generation within itself, the only way in the regular rules to translate how Generation work to D&amp;D 5th would be either as a Background or an Origin Feat. And that would require enough balance between them that you don't feel one as a more optimized choice than the other. Or would need strict control by the GM on which Generation everyone will be at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T12:30:59-07:00","id":1562318,"title":"","content":"I guess they couldn't go without adding the d-word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T12:38:19-07:00","id":1562319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562316#post1562316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. Though not sure a lot of WoD characters can compare to the insane stunts of dnd high level mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can if you follow Shadowrun's advice and geek the mage first. Having super-speed and super-strength can help considerably there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're a special batch of complete nutty stunt. Granted I have a friend who's good at that so maybe my view is skewed. </div> </div> </div>Only if you let them cast stuff nearby. Most spells have a rather limited range, but throwing a sling bullet like a rifle bullet can go a lot further...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T17:22:42-07:00","id":1562324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562319#post1562319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can if you follow Shadowrun's advice and geek the mage first. Having super-speed and super-strength can help considerably there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Only if you let them cast stuff nearby. Most spells have a rather limited range, but throwing a sling bullet like a rifle bullet can go a lot further...</div> </div> </div> </div>Systems translation. Legacy WoD has extra actions because it's badly designed in this area and never thought it relevant enough to revise thoroughly, not because its denizens are faster. Same for basically everything.<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D a Celerity 5 would <i>in extremis</i> be about five nonadditive speed related spells. Good, but not game breaking.<br /> <br /> WoD is for games where the power disparity between characters is meant to be absolute, something you can only bridge by changing yourself at the metaphysical level. Yet a bad roll in a bad moment can flatline a Garou with a starting level sniper (or, as once I saw, a granny with an umbrella)<br /> <br /> D&amp;D is for games where four humans can, with experience alone, face the Archdukes of Hell and win. Where the Time of Judgment books are meant to be overcome by a ragtag band of misfits united 2 years ago to buy a carton of milk. They still didn't find the milk. And no amount of luck will one-shot a level 10th char with the resources of a 1st level one, period.<br /> <br /> Those aren't differences in power, they're differences in story conceptualization. In WoD a regular D&amp;D Wizard would be a Sorcerer, even if one built with more XP than Mithras probably never had, and would be at a fundamental disadvantage. But in D&amp;D few Elders would be above 8th level, some wouldn't reach 6th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T22:09:57-07:00","id":1562402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562324#post1562324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Systems translation. Legacy WoD has extra actions because it's badly designed in this area and never thought it relevant enough to revise thoroughly, not because its denizens are faster. Same for basically everything.<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D a Celerity 5 would <i>in extremis</i> be about five nonadditive speed related spells. Good, but not game breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which D&amp;D? pre-3e gives warriors attacks with an unmodified THAC0. 3e nerfs warriors into the ground by giving everyone a descending sequence of attacks, 4e does its own thing, and 5e gives several attacks at a much more modest Proficiency bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WoD is for games where the power disparity between characters is meant to be absolute, something you can only bridge by changing yourself at the metaphysical level. Yet a bad roll in a bad moment can flatline a Garou with a starting level sniper (or, as once I saw, a granny with an umbrella)<br /> <br /> D&amp;D is for games where four humans can, with experience alone, face the Archdukes of Hell and win. Where the Time of Judgment books are meant to be overcome by a ragtag band of misfits united 2 years ago to buy a carton of milk. They still didn't find the milk. And no amount of luck will one-shot a level 10th char with the resources of a 1st level one, period.<br /> <br /> Those aren't differences in power, they're differences in story conceptualization. In WoD a regular D&amp;D Wizard would be a Sorcerer, even if one built with more XP than Mithras probably never had, and would be at a fundamental disadvantage. But in D&amp;D few Elders would be above 8th level, some wouldn't reach 6th. </div> </div> </div> D&amp;D still rates most of the types of monsters that the WoD focuses on as being quite dangerous, though. And converting over the Attributes to Ability scores usually gets some pretty high collections of stats, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T23:10:00-07:00","id":1562412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562402#post1562402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which D&amp;D? pre-3e gives warriors attacks with an unmodified THAC0. 3e nerfs warriors into the ground by giving everyone a descending sequence of attacks, 4e does its own thing, and 5e gives several attacks at a much more modest Proficiency bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> D&amp;D still rates most of the types of monsters that the WoD focuses on as being quite dangerous, though. And converting over the Attributes to Ability scores usually gets some pretty high collections of stats, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, in a limited sense, but true. And I was referring to 5.5, but as far as Wizards are concerned it doesn't make as much of a difference.<br /> <br /> But comparing them directly is complicated to say the least. In 5th Ed a Vampire is CR 13, but a Werewolf is CR 3. And both have quite different stats from what a translated WoD version would have.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition the Vampire is CR +2, so It could be in theory as low as 2 (excluded minimum level and Vampire Spawns and using an NPC class). A Werewolf is wonkier, but minimum 3. And for the Vampire we're talking what would be like a Neonate with a lot of extra Discipline dots.<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, IIRC vampires are around CR 10 or 11. and between Werewolves, fairies, mages, ghosts, mummies and demons, they're in the top-tier (there are stronger demons, but again things get pretty wonky).<br /> <br /> In 3.5 a Neonate would likely be a Template over a regular 1st level Character, and would have less cool powers than the Vampire Spawn unless you decide to translate Celerity directly as that many extra attacks. It really wouldn't be all that strong.<br /> <br /> For a Garou I'd rather use the Dire Wolf for the template and add the smaller wolf form and Glabro as extras. But that would still be around CR 7. Higher potential with Gifts, but at Rank 1 there's nothing really increasing it a whole CR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T08:07:52-07:00","id":1562427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562293#post1562293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://marketplace.dndbeyond.com/category/4IQF87I?icid_medium=organic&amp;icid_source=editorial&amp;icid_campaign=2026_3p_&amp;icid_content=article_2216&amp;pid=DB4IQF87I\" target=\"_blank\">Released</a> yesterday, USD 30 on D&amp;D Beyond.<br /> <br /> There's also a <a href=\"https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2216-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-brings-the\" target=\"_blank\">preview</a> to tell what's inside.<br /> <br /> But as expected, clans as subclasses, and they avoided Tremere.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are apparently tied to clan and you need a feat to get Out of Clans.<br /> <br /> For those who just want a summary:<br /> <br /> 1. All main rules are Class traits. They include Blood Points, resisting the Beast, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. Six Clans: Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue.<br /> <br /> 3. Backgrounds and Feats, they included new Origin Feats. Thin Blood is a Feat for other characters rather than a Class.<br /> <br /> 4. Generation as an Epic Boon... Ok?<br /> <br /> 5. New equipment, nothing I found interesting except maybe the potion of Kindred Vitae.<br /> <br /> 6. Closes with an Adventure for Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> While it's probably compatible across the board, this is written under the assumption that you'll use WoD as setting, not a regular D&amp;D world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like V6... I kid, I kid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Seriously tho, sounds about right for VtM in D&amp;D, some people will like it I am sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T09:50:55-07:00","id":1562431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562427#post1562427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like V6... I kid, I kid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously tho, sounds about right for VtM in D&amp;D, some people will like it I am sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to read the actual material, just saw the blurb. But seems ok-ish at least.<br /> <br /> And I think a lot of diehard VtM fans would probably like it better, those who like combat rules working with a semblance of balance. A lot of players never really liked the Storytelling system, they just tolerate it for either lack of reference or pride.<br /> <br /> Not for me, I don't mind combat being unfair and secondary for this game, maybe some in my group will like, so I may try it anyway, but a lot of people here I think would actually like it if they're tried it and stopped trying to fit a square in a circle with hundreds of house rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T13:19:29-07:00","id":1562439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562412#post1562412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, in a limited sense, but true. And I was referring to 5.5, but as far as Wizards are concerned it doesn't make as much of a difference.<br /> <br /> But comparing them directly is complicated to say the least. In 5th Ed a Vampire is CR 13, but a Werewolf is CR 3. And both have quite different stats from what a translated WoD version would have.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition the Vampire is CR +2, so It could be in theory as low as 2 (excluded minimum level and Vampire Spawns and using an NPC class). A Werewolf is wonkier, but minimum 3. And for the Vampire we're talking what would be like a Neonate with a lot of extra Discipline dots.<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, IIRC vampires are around CR 10 or 11. and between Werewolves, fairies, mages, ghosts, mummies and demons, they're in the top-tier (there are stronger demons, but again things get pretty wonky).<br /> <br /> In 3.5 a Neonate would likely be a Template over a regular 1st level Character, and would have less cool powers than the Vampire Spawn unless you decide to translate Celerity directly as that many extra attacks. It really wouldn't be all that strong.<br /> <br /> For a Garou I'd rather use the Dire Wolf for the template and add the smaller wolf form and Glabro as extras. But that would still be around CR 7. Higher potential with Gifts, but at Rank 1 there's nothing really increasing it a whole CR.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then, CR is largely meaningless and stacked in ways that don't guarantee that it means what it's supposed to. In 3.x in particular, there's a difference between CR, LA, and ECL, while in 5e, CR just turned outright into a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T14:42:06-07:00","id":1562445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560713-d-d-and-vtm-vampire-the-masquerade-bound-by-blood-5-5e?p=1562439#post1562439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, CR is largely meaningless and stacked in ways that don't guarantee that it means what it's supposed to. In 3.x in particular, there's a difference between CR, LA, and ECL, while in 5e, CR just turned outright into a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, but that's not the point.<br /> <br /> What matters is that this is not a simple translation. Saying that you need high levels to represent WoD splats misses what the translation is really about.<br /> <br /> Not that the result will be weak or anything. But not that powerful unless deliberately made to be powerful for no return.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the bad part about 5th Ed is that it has to deliberately made everything weak to be playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}